{
  "_comment": [
    "Hand-authored expectations for the cross-reader check. These values are",
    "written by a person from the fixture, NOT generated from the producer's",
    "output: a table derived from the writer would agree with the writer by",
    "construction and could not witness anything.",
    "",
    "Addressing is by INDEX inside sequences, never by matching on a field value.",
    "A selector like components[id=12345] would itself depend on that id surviving",
    "as a string, so when quoting breaks the lookup fails and the failure reads as",
    "'path missing' instead of 'wrong type'. Indices keep the diagnosis honest.",
    "",
    "Mappings are the exception, and it is a real limitation rather than a choice:",
    "technologies and connection_stacks are keyed by id, so those two paths address",
    "through a map key. If a writer ever mangled a map key, these entries would",
    "report 'absent' rather than naming what happened. Map keys are not schema",
    "paths and are out of scope here; see tests/CROSS_READER_CHECK.md.",
    "",
    "schema_path records which classified path each entry covers, so the check can",
    "assert its own completeness against cross_reader_classification.json rather",
    "than trusting this file to be exhaustive. Completeness is two-way: every path",
    "the classification calls reachable must appear here, and every path here must",
    "be one the classification calls reachable.",
    "",
    "An entry with no type key asserts a string, which is the ordinary case and the",
    "reason the 48 string entries carry no annotation. The type key is only on the",
    "four numeric entries, and that polarity is deliberate: a new numeric path added",
    "without it is checked as a string and goes red, whereas the reverse convention",
    "would let a forgotten annotation pass unnoticed.",
    "",
    "The three integer entries are pinning a disagreement, not blessing one. The",
    "schema declares number for all four; the writer emits 2000.0 as 2000, so PyYAML",
    "resolves an int where yaml-cpp had a double. Those four are here because an",
    "import writes them; the other 24 numeric paths are not covered by this",
    "check."
  ],
