  "import_producer": {
    "_comment": [
      "The actual-producer positive. Everything above is about a document this",
      "check loaded and re-saved; that establishes agreement about a document",
      "RESEMBLING an import, not about what an import writes. This block drives",
      "chiplet_studio.write_single_gds_import, which is the same function",
      "src/ui/MainWindow.cpp calls, and puts its output through both readers.",
      "",
      "spec is INPUT and expect is OUTPUT, both hand-authored. thickness_um is",
      "deliberately ABSENT from the spec: 200 has to arrive from the C++ default",
      "constructor through py::init<>, so a changed default in ChipletSynth.h",
      "reddens this instead of leaving it green on a number nothing produces.",
      "",
      "These entries are OUTSIDE the coverage arithmetic above, deliberately.",
      "Folding them into expect would let an import entry for",
      ".components[].dimensions.width satisfy the two-way coverage assertion",
      "after the synthetic fixture's entry was deleted, and would inflate the",
      "48-of-48 figure with paths counted twice.",
      "",
      "What this does NOT witness: MainWindow builds the spec from the GDS",
      "bounding box and the import dialog, and nothing here sees that. The",
      "positive is about what the writer does with a spec, not about what the",
      "user's dialog hands the writer."
    ],
    "spec": {
